# Evaluating Behavioural Observation Audiometry with Handicapped Children.

**Authors:** Flexer, Carol, Gans, Donald P.

## Abstract
Three observers evaluated the responses to sound with 21 mild to severely handicapped children (7 months to 10 years old) on Behavioural Observation Audiometry, an alternative to conditioning paradigms in audiometric assessment. Results showed that inter-observer agreement was high and that responsitivity was not affected by stimulus presentation mode. (Author/CL)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ289764

